ff802-cc-auto (0.2.0~dev2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Development build, not released; for the practical test on the unit.
  * Mixer writes compiled in (FF802_ENABLE_MIXER_WRITE=ON, only in this
    package build): the ALSA sequencer write path was confirmed on the
    unit in the hardware tests B.2 (0x2600) and B.3 (0x4228, 0x4269).
    The automatic initialisation stays OFF after installation
    ('ff802-cc-auto mixer-init on' turns it on).
  * New program /usr/bin/ff802-mixer-init (--list, --dry-run, --apply):
    the same 24 register writes and flow as the service, by hand, with
    a SEND confirmation; also as 'ff802-cc-auto mixer-init dry-run|apply'.
  * 10 ms between the 24 messages and 200 ms before unsubscribing (as in
    B.3); waiting for card and MIDI port up to 15 s.

 -- Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

ff802-cc-auto (0.2.0~dev1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Development build, not released, not for installation on the
    production host. Built from the project tree after version 0.4.1.
  * Mixer initialisation in class-compliant mode (off by default,
    independent of the automation): 'ff802-cc-auto mixer-init on|off|status'
    with the root helpers ff802-cc-auto-mixer-on/-off and the polkit
    actions org.ff802cc.auto.mixer-on (administrator) and .mixer-off
    (active local user). When on, the service sets on every connection in
    CC mode the 24 fixed registers Playback 1..12 -> Output 1..12 and the
    volumes of Output 1..12 to 0 dB through the ALSA sequencer (MIDI port
    "Port 2" of the connection, found by card number), with one journal
    line per register, /run/ff802-cc-auto/mixer-result and, on failure,
    a separate desktop notification (mixer-event).
  * The mixer writes are NOT compiled in (FF802_ENABLE_MIXER_WRITE=OFF):
    the MIDI port is found and reported, nothing is sent ("disabled-build").
  * The service may now open ALSA device nodes (DeviceAllow=char-alsa rw);
    new dependency libasound2t64. The mode switch itself is unchanged.

 -- Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

ff802-cc-auto (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebuilt from project version 0.4.1 (ff802-cc-autoswitch reports
    0.4.1). License: MIT (copyright file in DEP-5 format), with a note
    that the project is not affiliated with RME.
  * No functional change: the program, the units, the udev rule, the
    polkit policy and the maintainer scripts behave as in 0.1.0/0.1.1.

 -- Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

ff802-cc-auto (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Documentation: README.Debian and the package description distinguish
    the automatic switch of this package (proprietary -> class-compliant
    only, never back, no port reset) from the manual switch of the
    separate package ff802-cc (enable with USB hub port reset, disable;
    disable is refused while the automation is on). No longer claims that
    switching back is not possible from Linux.
  * Rebuilt; no functional change: ff802-cc-autoswitch, the units, the
    udev rule, the polkit policy and the maintainer scripts behave as in
    0.1.0 (the program binary differs only because a shared USB backend
    structure gained a field used by ff802-cc disable; it reports project
    version 0.4.0).

 -- Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100

ff802-cc-auto (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package (T4): automatic switch of the original RME Fireface 802
    from proprietary USB mode (2a39:3fcd) to class-compliant mode
    (0424:3fdd) when it is connected or present at boot.
  * Off after installation; ff802-cc-auto on|off|status.
  * At most one attempt per USB connection; never resets the device,
    never retries, never switches back to proprietary mode.
  * Desktop notification in the Plasma session: reconnect the USB cable.
  * Not yet tested on the host (container development only).

 -- Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100
